Quiz: 5/5, was not familiar with Bluejacking/Bluesnarfing/Bluebugging so will review that course but otherwise this will be a quick one.

Bluetooth Attacks: Different vulnerabilities within Bluetooth connectivity. Insecure Pairing, Device Spoofing, and On-Path attacks are all examples here.
    Bluejacking: pranking/recon on a device by sending unwanted Bluetooth messages to a device.
    Bluesnarfing: Attempted unauthorized access to a bluetooth device to steal information.
    Bluebugging: Bluesnarfing but attempting to take over the device using bluetooth.
    Bluesmack: DDoS over bluetooth
    Blueborne: Targets devices over bluetooth, infects multiple devices at once.

